\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {3D chamber digital twin visualizations: lessons on gravity level and pump flow rate in the LEAF GBC1 flight chamber.} \textbf  {a}, 3D isometric perspective of the LEAF GBC1 growth chamber ($48 \times 33.67 \times 68\ \mathrm  {mm}$) showing the polycarbonate housing, internal baffles at $Z = \pm 8.5\ \mathrm  {mm}$, porous foam reservoir, 35~$\mu $m Nytex screen at $Y = 14.77\ \mathrm  {mm}$, and 164 growing seedlings under nominal lunar flight conditions ($0.166g$, $Q = 25\ \mathrm  {mL\,min^{-1}}$ Push). \textbf  {b}, Lesson 1: Gravitational scaling from Earth 1.0g (straight downward gravitropism and rapid statolith sedimentation) to Moon 0.166g (attenuated driving, wider $35^\circ $ dispersion, and tangential Nytex surface gliding) and microgravity 0.0g (loss of downward vector, stochastic waving, and contact thigmotropism; Supplementary Fig.~S1). \textbf  {c}, Lesson 2: Ventilation flow rates and boundary-layer gas dynamics: active Push mode ($Q = 25\ \mathrm  {mL\,min^{-1}}$, $g_{\mathrm  {bl}} = 13.4\ \mathrm  {mm\,s^{-1}}$, ethylene $< 0.1\ \mathrm  {ppb}$) producing slender, healthy shoots versus stagnant pump-off faults ($Q = 0$, $g_{\mathrm  {bl}} < 3\ \mathrm  {mm\,s^{-1}}$, ethylene $= 136.5\ \mathrm  {ppb}$) triggering the classic ethylene triple response (+85\% radial hypocotyl swelling, exaggerated apical hook curvature, and stunted root elongation; Supplementary Fig.~S2). \textbf  {d}, Longitudinal boundary-layer conductance profile $g_{\mathrm  {bl}}(z)$ through baffle windows. \textbf  {e}, Quantitative organ morphometric comparison matrix across gravity and ventilation permutations (Supplementary Figs.~S3--S5).}}{8}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:chamber_lessons}{{7}{8}{\textbf {3D chamber digital twin visualizations: lessons on gravity level and pump flow rate in the LEAF GBC1 flight chamber.} \textbf {a}, 3D isometric perspective of the LEAF GBC1 growth chamber ($48 \times 33.67 \times 68\ \mathrm {mm}$) showing the polycarbonate housing, internal baffles at $Z = \pm 8.5\ \mathrm {mm}$, porous foam reservoir, 35~$\mu $m Nytex screen at $Y = 14.77\ \mathrm {mm}$, and 164 growing seedlings under nominal lunar flight conditions ($0.166g$, $Q = 25\ \mathrm {mL\,min^{-1}}$ Push). \textbf {b}, Lesson 1: Gravitational scaling from Earth 1.0g (straight downward gravitropism and rapid statolith sedimentation) to Moon 0.166g (attenuated driving, wider $35^\circ $ dispersion, and tangential Nytex surface gliding) and microgravity 0.0g (loss of downward vector, stochastic waving, and contact thigmotropism; Supplementary Fig.~S1). \textbf {c}, Lesson 2: Ventilation flow rates and boundary-layer gas dynamics: active Push mode ($Q = 25\ \mathrm {mL\,min^{-1}}$, $g_{\mathrm {bl}} = 13.4\ \mathrm {mm\,s^{-1}}$, ethylene $< 0.1\ \mathrm {ppb}$) producing slender, healthy shoots versus stagnant pump-off faults ($Q = 0$, $g_{\mathrm {bl}} < 3\ \mathrm {mm\,s^{-1}}$, ethylene $= 136.5\ \mathrm {ppb}$) triggering the classic ethylene triple response (+85\% radial hypocotyl swelling, exaggerated apical hook curvature, and stunted root elongation; Supplementary Fig.~S2). \textbf {d}, Longitudinal boundary-layer conductance profile $g_{\mathrm {bl}}(z)$ through baffle windows. \textbf {e}, Quantitative organ morphometric comparison matrix across gravity and ventilation permutations (Supplementary Figs.~S3--S5)}{figure.caption.7}{}}
